# GUARDRAIL: build trees are 130+ MB each; an initial commit that includes them makes every later diff
# unusable and the repo unshareable. Everything below is regenerable from source + sdkconfig.
build/
*/build/
probe/*/build/
probe/*/artifacts/
probe/*/artifacts_host/
probe/*/bake/
probe/*/flagtest/
probe/*/asm_dbg/
probe/research/*/build/
probe/research/*/artifacts*/
# agent working copies: keep their FINDINGS.md, drop the duplicated trees
probe/research/*/src/
probe/research/*/main/
probe/research/*/tests/
probe/research/*/tools/
probe/research/*/CMakeLists.txt
probe/research/*/countdown.sh
probe/research/*/*.fs
probe/research/*/host
probe/research/*/bake/
# logs and sdkconfig churn
*.log
sdkconfig.old
# flash images are small and ARE evidence; keep probe-results/*.bin
# GUARDRAIL: the first commit carried 79 MB of probe build trees (each build.ninja is 6 MB) because the
# ignore only matched a directory literally named "build". Build trees are named build_p42, build_stub,
# build_lhu, build.P23-reused … Match the pattern, and keep evidence (RESULT.md, *.bin, *.dis) out of it.
probe/repl/build*
probe/results/*/build*
probe/*/build*
cache/objects/
# GUARDRAIL: the fetched documents (15 MB TRM PDF) and the generated .dis listings are derived artefacts —
# the cache rule says they must never be DELETED from disk, which is not the same as committing them. Both
# are reproducible (cache by refetch, listings by probe/repl/tools/disasm.sh), so keep them out of history.
cache/derived/
probe/*/probe-results/asm/*.dis
